%
% WHAT THIS SHEET IS -- AND IS NOT (the founder's rule, kept):
% NO notation stands on this sheet, and that is the honest state
% of the record. Nothing was composed over this performance:
% no arpeggio layer, no spine, no kit rides on it -- the founder's
% ruling after Proof No. 4: IF IT ISN'T IN THE PERFORMANCE, IT
% ISN'T IN THE TRACK. The ONE ground under it is the Sigma the
% founder ORDERED into this track's spec -- named, designed and
% measured in THE PRODUCTION block below, not hidden in the mix.
% The Paganini line stands in the prompt below, and the performance
% played it as part of its own body.
% The transcription of the performance itself -- violin line
% included -- is a SEPARATE PRODUCTION, still OWED, and no
% sheet for it has been fabricated.
% What the performance was told stands below, verbatim, ONCE --
% the single invariant prompt of the seed take and every
% continuation:
%   detroit bounce hip hop instrumental in F minor at 144 bpm, simple steady bouncing groove that repeats and builds slowly, deep rolling 808 bass, crisp drums with fast steady hi-hats, one violin playing a simple memorable repeating melody, sparse eerie piano chords, a blues harmonica answering in short phrases now and then, dusty vinyl warmth, one continuous live performance, the final third sits back to groove and piano only with a wide open pocket, closing on an open vamp, no flutes, no breathy pads
%
% THE SESSION: the whole chain -- 7 takes -- was born in
% ONE bridge process, every continuation conditioned on the preceding
% audio IN MEMORY. No take was resumed from disk; an interrupted chain
% is void by rule, and the session guard weighed this chain before
% the splice was allowed.
% Voided attempts set aside before this strike: 1 (void-attempt-1).
% THE WARM-UP: 1 leading take(s) were struck and
% DISCARDED -- their audio is nowhere in this program. The warm-up's
% own measured tempo: 71.8 BPM. The kept program
% opens at kept take 1 (29.94 s into the chain).
% THE PERFORMANCE: 7 takes struck, 179.6 s of kept
% program, each extension generated CONTINUED from the preceding audio
% (5.0 s of conditioning) -- the model plays through
% every join. The kept takes are spliced DIRECTLY: no crossfade,
% no RMS matching, no grid, no trim.
%
% THE JOINS, WEIGHED (native 32 kHz splice points, kept program):
% the program's own internal jumps read median 0.00934, p99 0.24823; the joins:
%   join 1 after take2 at 0:29.9: waveform jump 0.42447 (45.45x the median internal jump), level step -0.57 dB
%   join 2 after take3 at 0:59.9: waveform jump 0.26831 (28.73x the median internal jump), level step -1.27 dB
%   join 3 after take4 at 1:29.8: waveform jump 0.73462 (78.67x the median internal jump), level step +0.10 dB
